TITLE: Exposing Subject as Observable (After) - TypeScript
DESCRIPTION: Illustrates the practice of keeping a `Subject` or `BehaviorSubject` private within a service and exposing only its `Observable` counterpart using `asObservable()`. This prevents external components or services from directly calling `next()`, `error()`, or `complete()` on the subject, ensuring controlled state updates through dedicated methods. Requires RxJS Subjects and Observables.
SOURCE: https://github.com/avivharuzi/angular-best-practices/blob/main/README.md#_snippet_15

LANGUAGE: typescript
CODE:

```
export class CartService {
  private selectedItem: BehaviorSubject<CartItem | null> = new BehaviorSubject<CartItem | null>(null);

  readonly selectedItem$: Observable<CartItem | null> = this.selectedItem.asObservable();

  updateSelectedItem(item: CartItem): void {
    this.selectedItem.next(item);
  }
}
```

