TITLE: Avoiding Nested RxJS Subscriptions (Before) - TypeScript
DESCRIPTION: Demonstrates an anti-pattern in RxJS where one observable is subscribed within the subscription callback of another. This nested structure can make code harder to read and manage subscriptions effectively, potentially leading to memory leaks. Requires `rxjs` observables.
SOURCE: https://github.com/avivharuzi/angular-best-practices/blob/main/README.md#_snippet_5

LANGUAGE: typescript
CODE:

```
firstObservable$.pipe(
    take(1)
  )
  .subscribe(firstValue => {
    secondObservable$.pipe(
        take(1)
      )
      .subscribe(secondValue => {
        console.log(`Combined values are: ${firstValue} & ${secondValue}`);
      });
  });
```

